        "lesson_activity.key": "f4b3f507-6bdd-439a-a4ee-ac2392af602c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b289e427-d544-4b87-aa90-f298b237449f",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-list-alt\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Display**: Show “Lesson Extras” slide",
        "progression_name": "Lesson Extras"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b289e427-d544-4b87-aa90-f298b237449f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "f4b3f507-6bdd-439a-a4ee-ac2392af602c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f7ddc72f-1fd2-4b0b-821d-115b666054e4",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-list-alt\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Display**: Show “Reflect” slide\n\n**Reflect:** _Sketch a simple shape on your paper and imagine the code used to draw it. Can you write that code out next to the shape?_",
        "name": "Reflection"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f7ddc72f-1fd2-4b0b-821d-115b666054e4",
        "lesson_activity.key": "866b2762-aaf5-45d5-9d5c-6f00f9e998f7"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "754038a0-47a2-45cf-bd91-98f03b56360d",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Use this activity to enhance student learning. It can be used as an outside of class activity or other enrichment.\n\n**The Copy Machine**\n\n- Give students two pieces of paper\n- On one sheet draw a simple image, using straight lines only.\n- On the second sheet draw instructions for recreating that image commands to move straight and turn at various angles.\n- Trade instruction sheets and attempt to recreate the image using only the provided instructions."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "754038a0-47a2-45cf-bd91-98f03b56360d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "88338519-bbb9-4bab-addd-a86e7127930e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "0d79ab73-19ff-4642-90ad-a2869dfc597b",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "###Shapes & Landscapes (45-60 minutes)\n![](https://images.code.org/5066103b929a2811e50d5bd54fbb114e-elaSmall.png)\n![](https://images.code.org/6a1508aeb443e243f595f88ecfa9ed7a-mathSmall.png)\n![](https://images.code.org/54b84cd74790e8e37daeff6cd826c185-scienceSmall.png)  **Computer Science + English Language Arts + Math + Science**\n\n\n[Shapes & Landscapes](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cPejd3i4v1A6iTMDtyOvlOfTVU9nlMg21bovwFThvvc/edit#) is an optional activity aligned to Common Core ELA, Common Core Math and Next Generation Science Standards, written by our teacher community. Students are asked to design a dam to prevent future flooding. Using code, you will create a blueprint to show the local town council how your dam will look.\n\n*Standards Addressed:*\n\n- **CCSS.ELA-LITERACY.W.2.8:** Recall information from experiences or gather information from provided sources to answer a question.\n\n- **CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.2.MD.A.3:** Estimate lengths using units of inches, feet, centimeters, and meters.\n- **NGSS.2-ESS2-1:** Compare multiple solutions designed to slow or prevent wind or water from changing the shape of the land.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "0d79ab73-19ff-4642-90ad-a2869dfc597b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "167e90cb-5767-4079-9f00-423d6f623eac"
      }
    }
  ],
